extraction_notes: |
  - Triax and the NGR, printed 200-201. The entry opens with a Data Note -
    "All other information is the same as the gargoyle" - so habitat, life
    span, enemies and allies are the Gargoyle row''s and are not repeated.
  - THE SURVEY LEFT THE EARTH ELEMENTAL SPELLS AS AN OPEN QUESTION AND THE
    ANSWER IS THAT THE CATALOG COVERS THEM. Its extraction plan said to check
    whether the existing warlock spell rows cover levels 1-3 before granting
    anything, because a grant with no gate is the F7 shape the Time Master
    import refused. Queried against production on 2026-09-06: the catalog holds
    exactly 29 `Earth:` spells at levels 1-3, and all 29 are granted here BY
    NAME. Nothing is invented and nothing is left ungated.
  - AND THAT LIST WILL ROT, in the same way and for the same reason as the
    Gypsy Gifted''s healing powers. An `Earth:` spell of level 1-3 imported
    later is NOT granted to this class until it is added here. Naming them is
    still better than a count: the mage POSSESSES all of them rather than
    picking any, so a count would turn a grant into a choice the book does not
    offer. `spells_starting` is 0 for exactly that reason.
  - THE FOURTH-LEVEL-WARLOCK PROFICIENCY IS NOT STORED. The entry casts these
    spells at a fixed proficiency regardless of the character''s own experience
    level, and the app has no per-spell proficiency; it is in `restrictions`
    where a player will meet it.
  - "+3 ON ALL OTHER SAVING THROWS" IS WRITTEN OUT, as on the Gargoyle Lord.
    `spell_magic` takes the +4 the entry prints for magic; the other thirteen
    d20 saves take +3; `horror_factor` takes its own +12; `coma_death_pct` is
    excluded as a percentage rather than a d20 bonus. RITUAL MAGIC IS THE ONE
    JUDGEMENT CALL: the entry says "+4 to save vs magic" once, and this catalog
    splits that into `spell_magic` and `ritual_magic`. It is stored at +3, on
    the literal reading that ritual magic falls under "all other saving
    throws"; a reader who thinks the book means both at +4 has a fair case and
    the difference is one point on one save.
  - THIS ENTRY DOES NOT GRANT LANGUAGE: GARGOYLE, and that is transcribed
    rather than corrected. Its skill list names Dragonese/Elven and Gobblely at
    98% where the common gargoyle, the gurgoyle and the lord all name Gargoyle
    as well. The Data Note says other information is the same as the gargoyle,
    but a skill LIST is information the entry states in its own right, so the
    omission is left standing and recorded here instead of being quietly
    patched.
  - FIVE PHYSICAL ATTACKS OR FOUR MAGIC ATTACKS - the app holds one number of
    attacks, so the physical five is stored and the alternative is in
    `restrictions`.
  - An absent ladder on printed 224 is not a verdict: this R.C.C. states that
    player characters use the DRAGON''s table, which resolves in this catalog.
    Nothing is stored - a Rifts class carries no `xp_table` here.
  - The secondary skills are twelve at +10% from ANY category - this entry
    excludes none, where the other four gargoyle R.C.C.s exclude four
    categories each. The +10% is not enforced, because `secondary_skills` holds
    a count and a schedule and a category `bonus` there is a parse error by
    design.
  - `psionics.type` is deliberately absent, for the reason recorded on the
    Gargoyle. This entry states no psionic tier and no psionic save target.
  - `magic.type` is `elemental`, which is one of the four kinds the parser
    knows and is what the book describes - a natural link to elemental forces
    rather than study.
