# Gargoyle Mage

## Lore

The gargoyle mage is endowed with natural magic abilities through a supernatural link with elemental forces. These powers are similar to the human elemental warlock''s, except that its magic is limited to one specific area: Earth. Those powers, and the lord''s ability to turn into living stone, suggest that gargoyles are somehow related to elementals - possibly lesser elementals themselves, or cousins to elemental beings. Whatever the connection is, it is unknown to the gargoyles. They accept their powers without question, and their history offers no clues.

The mage is a rarity: only about one in every 20,000 gargoyles. They look exactly like a typical gargoyle and can be of either sex. The mage is often the smartest and most charismatic of the clan and uses that to its advantage. It can become the Ultimate High Lord of a flock, but more often chooses to serve as advisor to the King - not out of submissiveness but out of cunning. Frequently it is the mage advisor who is the real power behind the throne, manipulating the more physically powerful lord or using his voice to enforce the mage''s edicts.

The gargoyle mage is also one of the few gargoyles to show great independence. Mages have been known to leave a flock and establish their own kingdoms among non-gargoyles - usually small kingdoms of goblins, kobolds, orcs and other creatures of low intelligence and warlike ways, where the mage is worshipped or feared as a god or demon lord. There have even been incidents where a village or tribe of humans or D-bees accepted a gargoyle as their ruler or god.

## GM Notes

A mage usually keeps a handful of subservient gargoyles (2D4) and gurgoyles (3D4) as a trusted guard and seconds in command, and the number can run lower or much higher and may include a few gargoylites or other demonic minions. These splinter groups are usually fairly small, although the kingdom they rule can be comparatively large. Gargoylites are one of the mage''s favourite minions, used for reconnaissance, spying, theft and assassination.

The average NPC mage ranges from 1D4+1 levels of experience, but can be lower or much higher; an experienced mage is 2D4+2. The highest level characters are incredibly dangerous, possess powerful magic, wield magic and rune weapons, and are likely to command a legion of gargoyles and gurgoyles. A mage can amass a fortune in magic items, gems and precious metals.

Everything else about this creature - habitat, life span, enemies, allies, how Europeans treat it - is the common Gargoyle''s. See that class.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gargoyle-mage');


